by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7729333-2bda-403b-82e6-858fa75ba2e3)\n\nI would like to request a feature that displays real-time token usage within Copilot Chat input field. Since each language model has its own context window and an optimal token count threshold, being able to see how many tokens have been consumed at any point in the conversation or coding session would be incredibly valuable.\n\nKey Benefits:\n\t1.\tPerformance Insights: Monitoring token usage helps users stay within the model’s sweet spot—avoiding sudden drops in response quality when the token count approaches or exceeds the context window limit.\n\t2.\tInformed Decisions: A token tracker clarifies when to truncate or reorganize prompts, preventing users from inadvertently degrading performance.\n\nProposed Implementation:\n\t•\tDisplay the current token usage (e.g., “Tokens used: X”) in a fixed position within the user interface (e.g., near the prompt bar or conversation history).\n\t•\tProvide a color-coded or visual meter that indicates when the usage is nearing critical levels based on the selected models max token window.\n\t•\tOptionally, allow users to set custom alerts or thresholds per model so they can be proactively warned of approaching limits.","closed_by":{"login":"roblourens","id":323878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzg3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens","html_url":"https://github.com/roblourens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roblourens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.g